(honking)

00:00:29.661 --> 00:00:32.411
(sirens blaring)

00:00:36.643 --> 00:00:37.476
- [Interviewer] All right.

00:00:37.476 --> 00:00:38.309
- Okay. (chuckling)

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:39.142
- [Interviewer] Kenzie?

00:00:39.142 --> 00:00:39.975
- Mm hm.

00:00:39.975 --> 00:00:40.808
- [Interviewer] Kenzie, where
are you from originally?

00:00:40.808 --> 00:00:41.641
- Phoenix, Arizona.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:42.820
- [Interviewer] Phoenix,
you've been out here how long?

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.510
- About four, a little over four years.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:45.463
- [Interviewer] Four years.

00:00:46.452 --> 00:00:47.285
- Hm mm.

00:00:47.285 --> 00:00:49.320
- [Interviewer] What
were the circumstances

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.953
that got you down here?

00:00:50.953 --> 00:00:53.920
- Hm, I actually was
brought down from Phoenix by

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.523
a guy who I later found out was a pimp.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:00.150
He...

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:01.060
Brought me down here,

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.930
promised me that like I was
gonna live in a nice house

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.800
and like he was gonna
take care of everything

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.130
and I'm a heroin addict and he was like

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:09.280
I can give you all the heroin you need.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:11.300
And then I was like, cool

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.133
and he had a few other girls with him

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:14.050
and they were like,
yeah everything's great

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.040
it's fine, it's fun.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:18.278
And then, so we drive down.

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:19.980
And end up in Compton,

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.249
I still don't remember
the exact streets but

00:01:22.249 --> 00:01:25.730
he pulls up to this like shack house

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:28.420
like shanty house, like they
had in like New York City

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.840
during like the Great Depression.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.240
Like it's made out of like..

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:36.620
Big pieces of wood like
nailed together and like

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:40.100
this like tarp as a roof and like

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.090
the first thing that I noticed
was like that there was...

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:45.270
the lock on the front door was backwards.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:47.090
And then all the locks in
the rooms were backwards.

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:48.040
They didn't lock from the inside,

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.800
they locked from the outside.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.100
And then like, I was like,

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.890
so I'm starting to get
sick, like what's up

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:54.450
and then, that was first time he hit me,

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:55.900
he slapped me across the face and he said,

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:57.550
bitch, I don't know what you think this is

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.480
but this is not like, I'm not giving...

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:00.820
You aren't given anything here.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.360
He was like, I'm gonna take you over

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.790
and I'm gonna put you on the
corner and you're gonna work.

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.720
And I said, okay...

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:07.737
Um, all right.

00:02:07.737 --> 00:02:09.200
And I just knew I was...

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.308
And from there I was
in really big trouble.

00:02:12.308 --> 00:02:13.141
- [Interviewer] How old were you then?

00:02:13.141 --> 00:02:15.396
- Uh, I was about 22.

00:02:15.396 --> 00:02:19.550
I stayed with him for
about two and a half weeks,

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:21.490
with him like, just giving
me a little taste of the dope

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:23.260
here and there, really sick.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:26.220
All my money I gave to him every night.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.260
Any time I like...

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:29.510
He just beat the crap out of us

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:30.890
every time he just felt like it

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:34.143
or he was upset or he thought
we were being disrespectful.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:38.600
Like, he was just a
horrible, horrible person.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:42.120
He would lock us in the
house all day, all night

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.297
until he wanted us to go work

00:02:43.297 --> 00:02:45.683
and then take us out over to Van Nuys.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:50.970
And then, about two and
a half weeks into it,

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:54.490
I got into a car with an
undercover police officer,

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:57.590
turned out to be and I
ended up getting arrested

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:00.700
off Sepulveda and Victory in Van Nuys

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:02.210
and..

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:04.560
I went to jail and I never saw him again.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:05.470
I asked the girls in jail

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:07.150
where I could get heroin really easily

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:09.980
and like, where I could go and

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:12.130
they told me how to get downtown,

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:14.071
to downtown Los Angeles and

00:03:14.071 --> 00:03:16.820
I just remember getting off the train

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:19.160
and being really sick and
walking up four streets

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:20.910
and seeing the tents and being like

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.810
What is going on?

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:26.530
What the he... whoa!

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:27.739
This is insane.

00:03:27.739 --> 00:03:28.927
- [Interviewer] It's crazy.

00:03:28.927 --> 00:03:29.760
- Hm mm

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:30.907
and I've here ever since.

00:03:30.907 --> 00:03:32.250
- [Interviewer] Had
you ever picked up guys

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:33.930
to make money before you met him?

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:35.482
So that was....

00:03:35.482 --> 00:03:36.315
- No, I --

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:37.398
- [Interviewer] An introduction.

00:03:37.398 --> 00:03:38.890
- Yeah, I was just walking
down the street in Phoenix,

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:41.050
just like, I don't know,

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:43.092
just screwing around
with my friends, I think.

00:03:43.092 --> 00:03:44.484
- [Interviewer] But,
you were doing heroin?

00:03:44.484 --> 00:03:45.490
- Hm mm, yeah.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:47.360
I was doing heroin and I was homeless,

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.517
I was just like

00:03:48.517 --> 00:03:50.910
doing random boosting or whatever.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:51.840
I had had a boyfriend

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:54.040
who had taken care of
me for a long time so.

00:03:54.978 --> 00:03:57.220
- [Interviewer] What age
were you when you started?

00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:58.810
- I was 16 when I started heroin,

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:01.786
I was 14 when I started getting high.

00:04:01.786 --> 00:04:03.850
- [Interviewer] Tell me
about your childhood.

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:06.540
- I grew up really, really poor.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.643
I'm the oldest of five kids.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:11.760
My dad is an alcoholic,
my mom is a drug addict

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.580
and they were really, really absent

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:15.677
as we were growing up like..

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:20.710
I raised my siblings like

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:24.910
until I was like 18 and I left.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.100
I was the one who like got them up

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.230
for school in the mornings,

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:28.269
made sure they ate dinner,

00:04:28.269 --> 00:04:31.020
when we had food I'd
make sure they ate dinner

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:31.853
Yeah.

00:04:31.853 --> 00:04:32.900
- [Interviewer] You were a
teenager, you were the parent.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:34.753
- Yeah, yeah, definitely.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:39.760
My parents, basically
after the kids were like

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:41.440
newborns or whatever like they would just

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.180
stop showing up at home like

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:47.310
like for days at a time
we couldn't find them.

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:49.170
Like the power would get shut off

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:51.330
every month after like about a week or so

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:52.569
cause my grandparents would..

00:04:52.569 --> 00:04:54.650
We'd have to call my
grandparents cause like

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:56.260
we'd be like literally starving

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.740
and like we wouldn't know where they were

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:00.960
so we'd have to call my grandparents,

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.040
they would track down my parents

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:03.740
my parents would come
back for like a few days

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.220
play the parent role or whatever

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:07.660
and then disappear again
for the rest of the month.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:08.493
So..

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:10.493
Yep.

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:13.420
- [Interviewer] Do you still have contact

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:14.640
with your siblings?

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.860
- Um, not really just
cause I'm getting high

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:21.210
and I don't want.. I've
like cause enough like

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:22.998
turmoil and like heartbreak and

00:05:22.998 --> 00:05:25.210
like worry in their lives,

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:27.130
like not until I get sober again.

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:28.003
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:05:30.044 --> 00:05:31.320
Where are you staying now?

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:32.153
Where do you sleep?

00:05:32.153 --> 00:05:35.301
- I stay in a tent off of Crocker and 7th.

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:36.134
- [Interviewer] Are you?

00:05:36.134 --> 00:05:38.210
- Yeah, um, I was staying
off 6th and St. Julian

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:40.664
and then about a month ago
my boyfriend went to jail

00:05:40.664 --> 00:05:42.650
and then I went to jail about two days..

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:44.480
a day later or whatever.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:46.410
And then when I got out, all
our stuff was gone again so.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:49.890
I got a new tent and then
I put it up over there.

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:50.723
So..

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:54.430
- [Interviewer] And then, what
are you doing for money now?

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:55.480
- Working the street.

00:05:57.394 --> 00:05:58.582
- [Interviewer] You
typically do that at night

00:05:58.582 --> 00:05:59.684
or during the day or?

00:05:59.684 --> 00:06:01.713
- At night, at night mostly, yeah.

00:06:02.819 --> 00:06:04.830
- [Interviewer] And how much
money do you make in a night?

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:06.210
- Like nothing (chuckling)

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:07.680
like about...

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:11.060
Like on a really good night,
I'll make like 120 bucks.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:14.310
On like a usual night
downtown, I'll make like

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:15.883
50, 60 bucks, that's it.

00:06:16.913 --> 00:06:17.746
- [Interviewer] And
you make sure everybody

00:06:17.746 --> 00:06:18.579
is using condoms and--

00:06:18.579 --> 00:06:19.500
- Always, always.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:20.333
I don't wanna,

00:06:20.333 --> 00:06:22.890
I would say I don't wanna
permanent consequence

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:24.790
off a temporary situation.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:27.640
You know, I don't wanna
end up with HIV or AIDS.

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:29.120
I'm only 26.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:30.760
Like I don't wanna end up with HIV

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:33.030
like I still have the rest
of my life you know like

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:34.820
and it's really prevalent down here.

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:37.150
I know like a couple
girls who have gotten HIV

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:38.750
like since I've been out here

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:41.653
and like, that's scary, that's horrible.

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:46.600
- [Interviewer] Where would you like to

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:47.433
be in five years you think?

00:06:47.433 --> 00:06:49.013
And what would you like to see now?

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:52.572
- Five years I would like to be like

00:06:52.572 --> 00:06:53.405
I don't know,

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:57.100
happy, just happy and comfortable

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:00.490
and like safe and secure like

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:02.203
that's really it.

00:07:02.203 --> 00:07:03.790
Like I don't like care where I'm working

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:06.570
or what I'm doing as long
as I'm happy, you know.

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:07.780
And like around people who like

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.350
really genuinely care for me.

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:11.770
Cause around here, nobody
really cares about you.

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:14.437
People just want what they
can get from you and..

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:16.910
There's a price to pay for everything.

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:19.543
Nothing around here is
free, that's for sure.

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:21.833
Especially for--

00:07:21.833 --> 00:07:22.880
- [Interviewer] What do
you think it is about

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.260
heroin addiction that blocks you from

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:27.610
getting your life together,

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:29.621
getting, taking some
responsibility, getting a job

00:07:29.621 --> 00:07:31.750
getting a place to live,
getting a car or whatever.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:34.667
Does it just drain your
energy to do that or you're..?

00:07:34.667 --> 00:07:37.170
- No, it just, it always comes first,

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:38.850
because you get dope sick or whatever,

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:41.870
just no matter what, the
dope comes before everything

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:44.320
because you're just so
afraid of getting sick.

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:46.210
Because once you get
sick, then it's over with,

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:47.560
you can't function, you can't hustle,

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:49.830
you can't get money,
you can't do anything.

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:50.663
- [Interviewer] Can't get dressed.

00:07:50.663 --> 00:07:52.010
- Yeah, you can't do anything.

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:53.015
Like you're literally like

00:07:53.015 --> 00:07:55.620
horribly, horribly sick.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.310
So you'll do anything to make sure

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:58.570
you don't get to that point.

00:07:58.570 --> 00:08:01.870
So like, if you have
to go to work that day

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:06.090
and you're outta dope and you
don't get paid till Friday

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:07.102
you gotta figure out something today

00:08:07.102 --> 00:08:10.110
like forget Friday, you know.

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:11.820
It's too much of a minute by minute,

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:12.850
day by day drug, you know.

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:14.423
- [Interviewer] Did you ever overdose?

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:20.280
- No, but I have like,
resuscitated and narcan

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:23.580
over like 15 people down here
since I've been down here.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:24.413
- [Interviewer] Okay.

00:08:24.413 --> 00:08:25.246
- Mm mm.

00:08:25.246 --> 00:08:27.790
- [Interviewer] Now,
Fentanyl is that something

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:29.291
you have to worry about with heroin?

00:08:29.291 --> 00:08:30.870
- Yeah, it's horrible,

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:31.703
cause these people like,

00:08:31.703 --> 00:08:33.340
like I try to tell people like

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:36.520
Fentanyl in the hospital
is for patients who are

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:38.950
terminally ill, who are about to be..

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:42.490
About dying, who are dying and
about to be, you know, dead.

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:44.770
And, it's measured in micro grams,

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:46.470
it's not measured in regular grams like

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:48.905
people don't understand that,
and it's like an anesthetic

00:08:48.905 --> 00:08:51.320
like a puts you asleep
or whatever for surgery.

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:52.380
It's like one of those drugs,

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:54.200
it's not meant to get high off of,

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:56.660
it's not, I've never watched
someone snort something

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:57.493
and overdosed.

00:08:57.493 --> 00:08:58.830
Like that, that was crazy to me,

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:00.610
this guy snorted some of it and overdosed.

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:03.610
We had to narcan him and do CPR like

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:05.763
that was insane like

00:09:05.763 --> 00:09:07.590
it's not something to mess around with

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:10.740
and then people are like playing chemistry

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:11.573
with the do..

00:09:11.573 --> 00:09:12.920
With the heroin and
then putting it in there

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:14.840
to make it like a little bit stronger

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:17.400
so they can make more money
and it's killing people.

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:19.330
And they just don't care.

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:21.012
It blows my mind.

00:09:21.012 --> 00:09:22.496
- [Interviewer] Did you
have dreams as a young girl

00:09:22.496 --> 00:09:24.310
of doing something with your life?

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:26.268
- I did ballet for like 12 years.

00:09:26.268 --> 00:09:28.450
And I always wanted to
got to like Julliard

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:30.160
or be a ballerina and then

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:32.340
if that didn't work out I
was gonna be a nurse and

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:33.190
like help people,

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:37.970
but I don't know, I just got so like

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:41.525
after like, like raising
my siblings and like

00:09:41.525 --> 00:09:43.040
nobody told me like

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:44.830
hey, fill out these college applications

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:47.750
or hey take this test or
hey, take these classes.

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:50.380
I didn't have any guidance
or any sort of direction

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:51.920
so I didn't end up doing any of it

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:54.170
and then I ended up getting
like hooked on these drugs

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:55.892
and then after that it was a wrap.

00:09:55.892 --> 00:09:57.475
It was just a wrap.

00:09:58.408 --> 00:10:01.158
(sirens wailing)

00:10:03.481 --> 00:10:04.511
- [Interviewer] Thank
you for talking to us.

00:10:04.511 --> 00:10:06.346
- Thank you, thank you.

00:10:06.346 --> 00:10:08.013
Thank you very much.

00:10:09.983 --> 00:10:12.762
Thank you, it will be a bright one.

00:10:12.762 --> 00:10:13.595
I've decided, it will be a bright one.

00:10:13.595 --> 00:10:15.928
(chuckling)

